  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Roll On Buddy Roll On** (1 other source): Listed as the encore [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **A Letter to Seymour**: rare: 9 archived performances [5]\n- **A Love Like Me**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2019-11-15.aud.c480b.ck63.nico11104.flac24** (recommended): audience recording; 25 songs; 137 min; rated 5/5 by 3 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Lineup credits Anders Beck on dobro, taking part remotely, Billy Failing on banjo and vocals, and Royal Masat on bass and vocals [1]\n- Relix webcast the show; this listener watched it, then attended the following night's show [4]\n- Listener found the next night's Brooklyn show, 11/16, otherworldly and hopes a recording of it surfaces [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2019-11-15.aud.c480b.ck63.nico11104.flac24**: taped by Fred Nicolois; transferred by Fred Nicolois; source: Aud>C483>F6 [1]. Also: Recorded with AKG C480B microphones with CK63 capsules, going into a Zoom F6 recorder [1]",
